# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CONVERA — Local development environment TEMPLATE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. Copy this file:    cp .env.local.example .env.local
# 2. Fill in real values from Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API
# 3. NEVER commit real keys — `.env.local` is gitignored.
# 4. If a real key was ever pasted into THIS file, rotate the key
#    and follow docs/secret_rotation_runbook.md.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Supabase project ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Replace YOUR_PROJECT_REF with the project ref from your Supabase URL.
# Use the STAGING ref for local dev; never paste production values here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co

# ─── Supabase API keys ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anon (publishable) key — safe to expose to the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<publishable-or-anon-key-placeholder>

# Service-role (secret) key — SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never expose to browser.
# Bypasses RLS; treat as production-equivalent secret even in dev.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<server-side-secret-placeholder>

# ─── Public deployment URL ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for email links, password-reset redirects, etc.
PLATFORM_BASE_URL=https://your-deployment.example.com

# ─── Test user (optional, scripts only) ──────────────────────────────
# Used by `npm run seed:auth-users`. NEVER commit a real password.
# TEST_USER_PASSWORD=PLACEHOLDER
